9, 13, 14 .","kind":"commentary","noteId":"tertullian-against-marcion-v-iv-3185"},{"text":"[^tertullian-against-marcion-v-iv-3186]: 1 Cor. vii. 27 .","kind":"commentary","noteId":"tertullian-against-marcion-v-iv-3186"},{"text":"[^tertullian-against-marcion-v-iv-3187]: One of Marcion’s Antitheses .","kind":"commentary","noteId":"tertullian-against-marcion-v-iv-3187"},{"text":"[^tertullian-against-marcion-v-iv-3188]: Viderint.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"tertullian-against-marcion-v-iv-3188"},{"text":"[^tertullian-against-marcion-v-iv-3189]: Et Christus: Pamelius and Rigaltius here read “Christi apostolus .” Oehler defends the text as the author’s phrase suggested (as Fr. Junius says) by the preceding words, “ Moses or Christ .” To which we may add, that in this particular place St. Paul mentions his injunction as Christ’s especially , οὐκ ἐγὼ, αλλ᾽ ὁ Κύριος , 1 Cor. vii. 10 .","kind":"commentary","noteId":"tertullian-against-marcion-v-iv-3189"},{"text":"[^tertullian-against-marcion-v-iv-3190]: 1 Cor. vii. 10, 11 .","kind":"commentary","noteId":"tertullian-against-marcion-v-iv-3190"},{"text":"[^tertullian-against-marcion-v-iv-3191]: 1 Cor. vii. 29 .","kind":"commentary","noteId":"tertullian-against-marcion-v-iv-3191"},{"text":"[^tertullian-against-marcion-v-iv-3192]: 1 Cor. vii. 39 .","kind":"commentary","noteId":"tertullian-against-marcion-v-iv-3192"},{"text":"[^tertullian-against-marcion-v-iv-3193]: 1 Cor. viii. 5 .","kind":"commentary","noteId":"tertullian-against-marcion-v-iv-3193"},{"text":"[^tertullian-against-marcion-v-iv-3194]: 1 Cor. viii. 4 .","kind":"commentary","noteId":"tertullian-against-marcion-v-iv-3194"},{"text":"[^tertullian-against-marcion-v-iv-3195]: 1 Cor. viii. 6 .","kind":"commentary","noteId":"tertullian-against-marcion-v-iv-3195"},{"text":"[^tertullian-against-marcion-v-iv-3196]: 1 Cor. iii. 21, 22 .","kind":"commentary","noteId":"tertullian-against-marcion-v-iv-3196"},{"text":"[^tertullian-against-marcion-v-iv-3197]: 1 Cor. iii. 23 .","kin